From: Timur Ravilov <93673987+t0b1kent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:37:15 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] JIT map on Windows: MACRUNNER_FEX_JITMAP_DIR and a working
 flush interval

FEX's perf-map writer (FEX_BLOCKJITNAMING, FEX_GLOBALJITNAMING, FEX_LIBRARYJITNAMING) opens
/tmp/perf-<pid>.map. Under Wine that path resolves inside the prefix. With
MACRUNNER_FEX_JITMAP_DIR=<Windows directory> (for example Z:\Volumes\Flash\jitmap) the map is
written there as fex-jitmap-<Windows pid>.map, so a host profile (macOS sample) can be
attributed to guest modules: block names carry "<guest module>+0x<offset>" through the ImageTracker.
The flush check compared LastWrite - Now against the threshold, which is always negative, so
buffers were written only when nearly full; it now uses the elapsed time.

Portions derived from FEX-Emu, Copyright (c) 2019 Ryan Houdek and FEX contributors, MIT License.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 FEXCore/Source/Common/JitSymbols.cpp | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Common/JitSymbols.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Common/JitSymbols.cpp
index 8e9341914..6f531f281 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Common/JitSymbols.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Common/JitSymbols.cpp
@@ -1,8 +1,10 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+// Modifications (c) 2026 MacRunner contributors, MIT
 #include <FEXCore/fextl/fmt.h>
 
 #include "Common/JitSymbols.h"
 
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 
@@ -17,6 +19,16 @@ JITSymbols::~JITSymbols() {
 
 void JITSymbols::InitFile() {
   // We can't use FILE here since we must be robust against forking processes closing our FD from under us.
+#ifdef _WIN32
+  // MacRunner: under Wine "/tmp" resolves inside the prefix (C:\tmp). MACRUNNER_FEX_JITMAP_DIR names a Windows
+  // directory, e.g. Z:\Volumes\Flash\jitmap, so the map lands on the host. The file name carries the Windows
+  // process id; the host pid is in the runner's pid map.
+  if (const char* Dir = getenv("MACRUNNER_FEX_JITMAP_DIR"); Dir && Dir[0]) {
+    const auto JitMap = fextl::fmt::format("{}\\fex-jitmap-{}.map", Dir, getpid());
+    fd = open(JitMap.c_str(), O_CREAT | O_TRUNC | O_WRONLY | O_APPEND, 0644);
+    return;
+  }
+#endif
 #ifdef __ANDROID__
   // Android simpleperf looks in /data/local/tmp instead of /tmp
   const auto PerfMap = fextl::fmt::format("/data/local/tmp/perf-{}.map", getpid());
@@ -131,7 +143,8 @@ void JITSymbols::RegisterNamedRegion(FEXCore::JITSymbolBuffer* Buffer, const voi
 void JITSymbols::WriteBuffer(FEXCore::JITSymbolBuffer* Buffer, bool ForceWrite) {
   auto Now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
   if (!ForceWrite) {
-    if (((Buffer->LastWrite - Now) < Buffer->MAXIMUM_THRESHOLD) && Buffer->Offset < Buffer->NEEDS_WRITE_DISTANCE) {
+    // MacRunner: elapsed time is Now - LastWrite; the upstream order made the time check always pass.
+    if (((Now - Buffer->LastWrite) < Buffer->MAXIMUM_THRESHOLD) && Buffer->Offset < Buffer->NEEDS_WRITE_DISTANCE) {
       // Still buffering, no need to write.
       return;
     }
